A||||4||Shaun41178||New oil pressure sender not working
Z||000000||Shaun41178||05-20-99||07:43 PM||||  i went out and bought a new oil pressure sender today because the guage in my car does not work.  Now just to let you all know I have an 85 GT and my car does not have the auxillary guages over the radio.  My oil guage is under the tach.<p>I bought the new unit at Autozone.  It is made by Wells and it cost me $29.  So I put the sensor on and the guage does not respond.  I wiggle the wires that plug into the sensor and still nothing<p>The needle in the dash is pegged all the way to the left.  It is pointing directly at the speedo and is at a 90 degree angle with the ground.  It is reading like I have less then 0 pounds of oil pressure.<p>Any suggestions as to what could be causing this?  Is it possible that the connector on the sennder has become corroded somehow?  I looked at it but it looked fine to me.  Is it possible that the guage in the dash is bad?  If so how do I go about fixing it?  Is there anything in particular that I should be looking for?  Anyone else have this same problem?  Thanks<p>
Z||000001||Pretender||05-20-99||10:23 PM||||i have almost the exactly the same problem but mine has the gauges over the radio, after i installed the oil sender unit it didn't work, after about two miles of driving it finally started to work!, then it cut out and has been dead ever since...stupid thing..
Z||000002||Phil||05-21-99||05:15 AM||||Check the resistance from the sender end of the wire to ground for a short. The sender itself should be 90 ohms to ground at max pressure. If all else fails I might have an extra gage kicking around from my 85
Z||000003||Phil||05-21-99||07:56 AM||||Was playing with my gage and found that if the tan wire from the sender is open the needle will peg, ground it and it goes to 0. Just might be the wire.
Z||000004||Shaun41178||05-21-99||02:54 PM||||Well i found the problem today and by accident.  <p>First i went out to start my car and it wouldn't start.  I had spark because my tach was jumping.  Poped the deckild and started palying with the oil pressure sender cause I thought it might have something to do with no fuel getting to the engine.  Playing with it the middle wire just popped out of the connector to the oil sender.  I looked at it and said well this has to be my problem right here.  I pushed the middle wire back in as far as I could and now the guage was responding when i put the key in the run position.  Car still would not start though<p>Turned my radio off and discovered that the fuel pump was not running.  Puuled the fuse and sure engouh it was gone.  popped a new fuse in and the car fired up and the oil guage was now sahowing a nice 80 psi.  Thanks god it was working.<p>Pretender I suggest you make sure that the wires going into the connector that connects to the sender are all the way in and not loose.  The middle one on mine was loose and actually popped out and I pushed it back in and now my guage is working.  I think this might be your problem too.<p>Thanks for the help guys although it was my sender connector the whole time and I didn't know it.
